liuqin: stub the macOS-only names IOHIDDevice.cpp references

0270 vendored Apple's IOHIDDevice.cpp unchanged. It references two things that
do not exist on iOS (and are not in this tree):

  IOHIDSystemActivityTickle(kind, this)   x2, in updateActivityTickle
  NX_HARDWARE_TICKLE                       the event kind constant

Both sit on the seize/tickle path: a real keyboard or pointing device being
seized by IOHIDSystem. This port has no IOHIDSystem layer at all and the
digitizer never seizes anything, so the correct behaviour is to do nothing.
IOHIDFamilyPrivate.h (also vendored, unchanged) declares the non-static
prototype, so the stub is a plain inline definition that satisfies it.
NX_NULLEVENT and the real IOHIKeyboard/IOHIPointing classes come from the
headers 0270 mirrors (IOLLEvent.h, IOKit/hidsystem/IOHIKeyboard.h), so they
are not restated here any more.

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/LiuqinHIDMacOSStubs.h b/iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/LiuqinHIDMacOSStubs.h
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/LiuqinHIDMacOSStubs.h
@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+/*
+ * LIUQIN: the macOS-only IOHIDDevice.cpp dependencies, as no-ops.
+ *
+ * IOHIDDevice.cpp is Apple source (IOHIDFamily-1915.140.3) kept unchanged.
+ * What it uses that exists only in the macOS IOHIDSystem layer, which iOS
+ * does not have and this port certainly does not:
+ *
+ *   IOHIDSystemActivityTickle -- wakes the macOS-wide event system so it
+ *       re-evaluates idle time. No event system here; a tickle would only
+ *       cost a lock on a service that does not exist.
+ *   NX_HARDWARE_TICKLE -- the event kind passed to the tickle call. The
+ *       macOS value (IOLLEvent.h) is kept so a future port that grows a
+ *       real tickle sink needs no change here; nothing on this port reads it.
+ *
+ * IOHIDFamilyPrivate.h already declares the non-static prototype, so this is
+ * a plain inline definition, not a static one.
+ */
+#ifndef LIUQIN_HID_MACOS_STUBS_H
+#define LIUQIN_HID_MACOS_STUBS_H
+
+#ifndef NX_HARDWARE_TICKLE
+#define NX_HARDWARE_TICKLE      24
+#endif
+
+/*
+ * IOHIDSystemActivityTickle: on macOS this wakes the event system so it
+ * re-evaluates idle time. There is no event system here; do nothing.
+ */
+inline void
+IOHIDSystemActivityTickle(int kind, IOService *sender)
+{
+	(void)kind;
+	(void)sender;
+}
+
+#endif /* LIUQIN_HID_MACOS_STUBS_H */
